# Holds and stops: seats that can't block still get the impulse when they ask for it.
# Seating A B C D: A's prey is B, its predator D. C's prey is D, its predator B.
seed 5
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
seat D dave
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *12
library A "Iron Ward" *40
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *12
library B "Quick Feed" *40
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *12
library C "Signal Fire" *40
crypt D "Tomas Grey" *12
library D "Quick Feed" *40
start

A> draw crypt
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> draw crypt
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> draw crypt
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> draw 7
D> draw crypt
D> move D:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# By default C, who can't block a bleed on B, is passed automatically.
A> bleed "Vera Nightfall"
expect impulse B
B> pass
expect action bleed A resolution
A> resolve failure
A> unlock "Vera Nightfall"

# A hold, armed while B decides: C gets the impulse instead of being passed.
A> bleed "Vera Nightfall"
expect impulse B
reject:no-change A> hold
reject:no-change B> hold
C> hold
log public C asks the table to wait
expect holds C
reject:no-change C> hold
B> pass
expect impulse C
expect action bleed A blocks
# Playing a card keeps the hold; passing releases it.
C> play C:hand:1
expect impulse A
expect holds C
A> pass
expect impulse C
C> pass
expect holds none
expect action bleed A resolution
A> resolve failure
A> unlock "Vera Nightfall"

# Standing stops. C stops for its prey's and predator's actions: not for A's.
C> stop neighbours
A> bleed "Vera Nightfall"
B> pass
expect action bleed A resolution
A> resolve failure
A> unlock "Vera Nightfall"

# C stops for every action.
C> stop anyone
A> bleed "Vera Nightfall"
B> pass
expect impulse C
C> pass
expect action bleed A resolution
A> resolve failure
C> stop neighbours

# A late hold voids D's automatic pass: the round waits until the impulse comes round to D.
# Phase round order: A, prey B, predator D, then C.
C> autopass none
A> next
expect window phase minion
expect impulse C
D> hold
expect holds D
C> pass
expect impulse A
A> pass
expect impulse D
D> pass
expect window none
expect turn 1 A influence
C> autopass all

# Holding needs an open window.
reject:not-now C> hold

# On to D's turn: D is C's prey, so C's neighbours stop fires on D's bleed of A.
A> next
A> next
B> next
B> next
B> next
B> next
B> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
D> next
D> next
expect turn 4 D minion
D> bleed D:ready:1
expect impulse A
A> pass
expect impulse C
C> pass
expect action bleed D resolution
